# A `from` first on the next line is a new query for certain, even after `project` (D-037).
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | project a, b
from u | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..38
  PIPELINE@0..21
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    PROJECT_OP@9..21
      IDENT@9..16 "project"
      WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@17..18
        NAME_REF@17..18
          IDENT@17..18 "a"
      COMMA@18..19 ","
      WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@20..21
        NAME_REF@20..21
          IDENT@20..21 "b"
  WHITESPACE@21..22 "\n"
  PIPELINE@22..37
    IDENT@22..26 "from"
    WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
    NAME_REF@27..28
      IDENT@27..28 "u"
    WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
    PIPE@29..30 "|"
    WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
    TAKE_OP@31..37
      IDENT@31..35 "take"
      WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
      LITERAL@36..37
        LONG@36..37 "5"
  WHITESPACE@37..38 "\n"

error[DS0106]: missing `;` between statements
  --> query:1:22
  |
1 | from t | project a, b
  |                      ^ expected `;` here
2 | from u | take 5
  | ---- a new statement starts here
  |
  = help: end the statement with `;`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | project a, b;
    from u | take 5
which parses without errors
